# Which paths each build job of the release may supply (re-audit NEW-ROOT-2). The pack job merges the stage tars of every job into
# one tree and signs it; release/stage-owners.py refuses the merge when a tar holds a path outside its job's lines below,
# or a path that two jobs both supply. So a build script that a dependency of one job runs cannot put a program or a unit
# that root runs or the input service believes (turnstile, keycap, palmrest, their services, the udev rules, the callers table) into the signed bundle.
#
#   JOB PATTERN
#
# JOB is the matrix name in .github/workflows/release.yml (release/selftest.sh checks that the two agree). PATTERN is a path
# below opt/quire/current in the stage, or components.d/NAME.txt; `*` stands for any run of characters inside one path
# segment, `**` for anything. Every line names what the job's components install (release/build.sh and the installers it
# runs): add a line with the file when a component starts to ship a new one, or the pack stops.
#
# Each program the system manager starts and the input service or the other services believe has a job of its own (turnstile,
# keycap, palmrest), so nothing built beside one can reach another or its unit. Paths under system/ are copies slipway-apply
# places as root; the trust table system/etc/quire/desktop-callers.toml belongs to the session alone, and no other job's list
# holds a pattern that matches it. A user unit that a row of the table names (and the portal frontend's drop-in) is a plain
# system file under system/usr/lib/systemd/user, not a staged lib/systemd/user file that would be exported as a link, which the
# unit manager's judge reads as writable (release/build.sh plain_units).

